III. Results
A. Sizing Parameters
Figure 2a shows maximum payload mass variation with MTOW according to Wp = 0.30 · W1.03, also provided for
convenience in Table 3. This represents approximately isometric scaling, meaning that the ratio between the maximum
payload mass and MTOW is constant across the entire rotorcraft range, irrespective of propulsion and rotor type. This
is in agreement with the data on the conventional rotorcraft class [2], shown in Fig. 2b. This allometric relation can
be used during the preliminary phases of unmanned rotorcraft design to quickly estimate MTOW based on a given
maximum payload mass.
